ade away from it the Dutch  promptly and decisively crushed the  English Navy after this Davitt was at  the height of his popularity in power  and so sought to use this to settle a  dispute with the oranges who were led by  the young William of Orange  as such he implemented a law which meant  that Holland no longer recognized the  officer stat holder making it impossible  for William to have control of the  entire country should he rise to power  to put it mildly this upset the oranges  but there wasn't much they could do yet  things went south in 1672 when King  Louie the fourteen for France decided  that the Dutch Republic existence had  gone on for a bit too long and so he  invaded and things went poorly  for the Dutch very poorly so much so  that 1672 is referred to as the ramp er  which directly translates to a year  which in retrospect can safely be  described as being pants with the French  army rampaging through the country the  oranges demanded of its head and made a  failed attempt to assassinate him he  resigned the office of grand pensionary  but this wasn't enough since he could  potentially return and so the orangist  arrested of its brother went of it went  to visit him he was ambushed and killed  by a mob and said mob subsequently ate  him and his brother not all of them that  would be uncouth but they did cook and  eat some of them we know this from  several sources who described it as  actually being a fairly organized  display of cannibalism which is pretty  rare in the end he was killed because  the people of his country were in a  state of raw panic and the Dutch mob ate  him because they hated him he had kept  their rightful monarch away from power  and so they sought to humiliate him in  death and in case you're wondering the  reaction to the deaths in the Netherland  was that it was justified in the  Neustadt holder William quickly pardoned  everyone so if you only take one thing  away from this when leaders messed  things up royally by losi